Usage: agent-deck recall follow <session> --after <cursor|end> --jsonl [--status]
Frames: row, update, remove, status, delivery, resync_required (docs/recall-timeline.md). --v1 streams the slice-6 turn frames.
  -after string
    	Resume cursor from timeline or a prior follow frame; 'end' starts at the current end
  -harness string
    	With --transcript: claude or codex
  -jsonl
    	Stream newline-delimited JSON frames
  -status
    	Also emit status frames (verb, elapsed, tokens, current tool, footer facts) once a second while the session runs
  -transcript string
    	Read this Claude Code JSONL or Codex rollout instead of a session's
  -v1
    	Slice-6 output (turns with role/kind/text, turn frames) instead of rows
